widest bands observed in MOFs, with a valence-band dispersion of \(400\;\mathrm{meV}.\) In perfect single crystals, such a wide dispersion may be expected to give rise to band-like transport, which would result in high charge mobility. This is corroborated experimentally by TRMC and TOF measurements, which give an intrinsic charge mobility of \(0.2\;\mathrm{cm}^{2}\,\mathrm{V}^{-1}\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}\) for \(Z\mathrm{n}_{2}(\mathrm{T}\mathrm{T}\mathrm{F}\mathrm{T}\mathrm{B})\) .

