Panda et al. also targeted \(\pi{-}\pi\) stacking interactions to construct a series of 2D layered \(\mathrm{In}^{\mathrm{III}}\) isophthalate MOFs.[75] FET devices made from these materials showed no measurable charge mobility for a MOF that lacked \(\pi{-}\pi\) stacking interactions, whereas a drop-cast polycrystalline film of a structurally related material that featured \(\pi{-}\pi\) stacking between the 2D layers exhibited a charge carrier mobility of \(4.6\times10^{-3}\,\mathrm{cm}^{2}\,\mathrm{V}^{-1}\,\mathrm{s}^{-1}\) (Figure 7).

